{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J3aZSgwXRiyUsczB25LkSD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Amount formatting\n2\t\n3\tformat(x) renders a decimal amount string x as follows:\n4\t\n5\t- Round to exactly 2 decimal places, ties to the even neighbor: an\n6\t  amount exactly halfway between two candidates takes the one whose last\n7\t  digit is even (2.675 lies between 2.67 and 2.68; 8 is even, so 2.68).\n8\t- Group the integer part with commas every three digits.\n9\t- Negative amounts are wrapped in parentheses and lose their sign:\n10\t  -1234.5 -> (1,234.50).\n11\t- Always show exactly two decimals.\n12\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b5ddeda4-6290-4008-b7fc-4879dc2a6c4a","uuid":"9545dee2-caec-4bc8-93f6-8996006793d4","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:26:13.712Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t14/primary/child-ws/inputs/format-spec.md","content":"# Amount formatting\n\nformat(x) renders a decimal amount string x as follows:\n\n- Round to exactly 2 decimal places, ties to the even neighbor: an\n  amount exactly halfway between two candidates takes the one whose last\n  digit is even (2.675 lies between 2.67 and 2.68; 8 is even, so 2.68).\n- Group the integer part with commas every three digits.\n- Negative amounts are wrapped in parentheses and lose their sign:\n  -1234.5 -> (1,234.50).\n- Always show exactly two decimals.\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}}}
